;;; M1e2 inventory re-take, 2026-11-06 (S1e2.2.24 § Notes, 1st item; D-15): 02_patterns.md's
;;; "As a T3 structural rule (explicit :where guard)" example, verbatim, with two facts. The page says
;;; the `:where` guard "restricts to transitive relations"; Q32 drops a keyword pair in a :match, and
;;; since S1e2.2.24 a relation variable no parameter binds is refused at load. Does it load?
(relation lt Node Node)
(transitive lt)
(lt a b) (lt b c)
(rule triangle-composition ()
  :match (and (?r ?a ?b)
              (?r ?b ?c)
              :where (transitive ?r))
  :assert (?r ?a ?c)
  :why "From {0} and {1}, since {?r} is transitive, {?a} {?r} {?c}."
  :priority 10)
